$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3β -Acetoxy-14β ,15β -epoxy-5β -androst-17-en-20-one (20). Diene 13 (0.15
g, 0.42 mmol), and m-CPBA (75%, 0.127 g, 0.552 mmol) were dissolved in
CHCl3 (6 mL) and stirred at it for 2.5 h. A 0.5 M Na2S2O3 solution was
added and the resulting mixture was partitioned between-CH2Cl2 and NaHCO3
The organic layer was dried and concentrated to provide 0.156 g (100%) of
epoxide 20 as a white solid. 3β -Acetoxy-14β ,15β -epoxy-5β
-androst-17-en-20-one (20), yield (0.156 g, 100%) NMR (400 MHz): δ
0.90-2.40 (m, 17 H), 1.00 (s, 3H), 1.30 (s, 3H), 2.05 (s, 3H), 2.24 (s,
3H), 3.82 (d, J= 1.04, 1H), 5.05 (br s, 1H), 6.91 (s. 1H). 13C NMR (100
MHz): δ 16.80, 19.82, 20.77, 21.38, 23.57, 24.94, 25.62, 27.25, 30.03,
30.32, 33.26, 35.17, 36.47, 36.58, 38.84, 47.88, 59.24, 70.21, 74.88,
140.48, 158.11, 170.56, 196.25. The 1H NMR data is in good agreement with
the literature.6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
