$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Catalytic activity. In this study, Fe3O4/SiO2 NPs were tested to catalyze
the selective oxidation of alkenes using m-CPBA as an oxidant. Styrene
was selected as model substrate and treated with Fe3O4/SiO2 NPs in the
presence of m-CPBA as the oxygen donor at room temperature under
different conditions. This reaction was best carried out using 2 equiv.
of m-CPBA for 4 h at room temperature in dichloromethane. The catalytic
activity of the Fe3O4NPs was also investigated in the epoxidation of
styrene, and low yield (45 %) was observed. Blank experiments showed that
Fe3O4 and Fe3O4/SiO2 NPs alone are inactive towards the styrene
epoxidation. To optimize the amount of catalyst, the reaction was carried
out in the presence of different amount of Fe3O4/SiO2 NPs (0.01-0.08 g)
at room temperature. It was found that 0.06 g of Fe3O4/SiO2 was
sufficient enough. Styrene oxide with 97 % isolated yield, Catalyst
amount (g): 0.06, Temperature: 25 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, solid-supported catalyst, catalyst prepared and used,
ailica support used, optimization study, optimized on agent, solvent and
stoichiometry of catalyst, selectivity, (99%)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild oxidation of alkenes catalyzed by Fe3O4/SiO2 nanoparticles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nasseri, Mohammad Ali; Allahresani, Ali; Raissi, Heidar
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Reaction Kinetics, Mechanisms and Catalysis (2014), 112(2), 397-408

