$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.7 mmol triphenylmethyl substituted olefin,
0.042 g salen Mn (III) (about 15 mol%) and 5 mL CH2Cl2 were added into a
100 mL three-neck flask. At 0 °C 20 mL of a solution of DMD in acetone
(0.1 mol·L-1) was rapidly dropwise added. Upon addition, the reaction
mixture was warmed slowly to room temperature and further violently
stirred. The reaction process was traced by TLC. After 24 h, additional
20 mL solution of DMD in acetone (approx. 0.1 mol·L-1) was dropwise added
over 2 h by controlling the dropping rate. After that, the reaction was
further violently stirred at room temperature for 20 h. Upon completion,
the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue purified
by chromatography on silica gel column [developing agent: mixture solvent
of petroleum ether and ethyl ether (10 : 1, V : V)] to give a yellowish
solid. The resulting solid was recrystallized from a little n-hexane to
afford a white or colorless crystal. (Z)-5,5,5-triphenyl-2,3-epoxypentane
(4b), 98 %, white crystal m.p. 114-116 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ: 7.18-7.36
(m, 15H, ArH), 3.18 (dd, J = 14.6, 3.2 Hz, 1H, 3-CH), 2.94-2.98 (m, 1H,
2-CH), 2.80 (dd, J = 5.4, 9.8 Hz, 1H, cis CH2), 2.53 (dd, J = 7.2, 14.6
Hz, 1H, trans CH2), 0.87 (d, J = 5.5 Hz, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ:
146.79, 129.12, 128.01, 126.22, 55.73, 54.96, 54.09, 38.11, 13.01; MS
(FAB) m/z (%): 314.1 (M+, 100). Anal. calcd for C23H22O: C 87.86, H 7.05;
found C 87.98, H 6.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on reagent and time
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Study on the epoxidation of triphenylmethyl substituted olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Pan-Deng; Yang, Nian-Fa; Ling, Ying; Li, Ji-Chao; Cao, Jing
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Youji Huaxue (2007), 27(7), 885-889

