$DATUM 47.6 g (0.112 mol) ADI, 481.4 g (5.668 mol) dichloromethane, and 56.7 g
(0.329 mol) m-chloroperoxybenzoic acid (m-CPBA) were placed into a
three-necked round-bottom flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, a
thermometer, and a reflux condenser. The reactants were mixed and stirred
at 30 °C for 48 h. The solution was filtrated and washed with a solution
of 10% sodium sulfite followed by a solution of 10% sodium carbonate and
distilled water. The organic layer was then dried over anhydrous sodium
sulfate. The product was obtained after removing the dichloromethane
completely. The epoxy value of EADI determined by the hydrochloric
acid-acetone method was about 0.435. Phosphorus-containing bio-based
epoxy resin (EADI), Yield: 97.7%, 50.0 g (0.109 mol). 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
acetone-d6, δ ppm): 8.17 (m, 2H), 7.98 (m, 1H), 7.81 (m, 1H), 7.64 (m,
1H), 7.48 (m, 1H), 7.31 (m, 2H), 4.34 (m, 2H), 3.83 (m, 2H), 2.5-3.2 (m,
11H). 13C-NMR (400 MHz, acetone-d6, δ ppm): 172.44 (1C), 170.67 (1C),
149.03 (1C), 120-136 (11C), 65.49 (2C), 48.72 (2C), 43.65 (2C), 35.60
(3C).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
