$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of Tetrahydrothiophene in
Homogeneous Solution: A solution of magnesium monoperphthalate
hexahydratc (MMPP) (37.5 g. 83% of theoretical available oxygen, 63mmol)
in H2O (150 mL) is added to a solution of tetrahydrothiophene (10.0 g,
114 mmol) in EtOH (20 mL) and the mixture kept at 50' C for 2 h. GLC
analysis shows that no starting material remains and that no
tetrahydrothiophene, S,S'-dioxide accompanies the tetrahydrothiophene
S-oxide. Trimethyloxirane, yield 98%. m.p or b.p, Found: 74-75 °C,
Reported: 75s °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidation reactions using magnesium monoperphthalate: a comparison with
m-chloroperoxybenzoic acid
