$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. To the solution of complex
Mn-2 (1.0 μmol, 0.68 mg) in CH3CN (0.4 mL) (or methanol, 0.5 mL),
thermostated at desired temperature, the substrate (200 μmol) was added
in one portion, and 250 μmol of AcOOH (or 250 μmol of HCO3H) was slowly
added within 3 min. The mixture was stirred for a desired period of time
(10 min up to 3h). Then 1.5 mL of saturated aqueous NaHCO3 was added and
the aqueous phase was extracted with pentane (3×2 mL). The solvent was
carefully removed in a stream of air, the residue was dissolved in 1.0 mL
CCl4 and dried over CaSO4. The mixture was filtered and the filtrate
analyzed by 1H NMR spectroscopy. The yield was calculated based on the
portion of the epoxide in the reaction mixture (for examples see Figure
S1). The concentrations of the products in reaction mixtures were
established based on comparison with the solutions of the starting olefin
of known concentration in the same solvent (CCl4 ). The admixture of
trichloroethylene (δ 6.46) in CCl4 served as a side reference for peaks
integration. A similar procedure was applied for catalysts Mn-3 and Mn-4.
The enantiomeric excess values were analyzed either by 1H NMR with a
chiral shift reagent Eu(hfc)3(for the epoxides of styrene,
trans-β-methylstyrene, 1,2-dihydronaphthalene, indene, 1-octene) or by
chiral HPLC (styrene epoxide, dbpcn epoxide). If organic hydroperoxides,
m-CPBA or iodosylarenes were used as oxidants, the
catalyst:substrate:oxidant ratio was 1:100:110. Entry no. 6; T, -20 °C;
time, 2 h; conversion, 97.5 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 35% ee, other products also detected, optimization
study, optimized on reagent and stoichiometry, mechanism studied,
alternatively reaction carried out at zero degree Celsius decreased
conversion
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nonheme Manganese-Catalyzed Asymmetric Oxidation. A Lewis Acid Activation
versus Oxygen Rebound Mechanism: Evidence for the "Third Oxidant"
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ottenbacher, Roman V.; Bryliakov, Konstantin P.; Talsi, Evgenii P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Inorganic Chemistry (2010), 49(18), 8620-8628

