$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for the Epoxidation of Alkenyl Ether (1f) To a solution of
alkenyl ether 1f (150 mg, 0.6 mmol) in MeCN (3 mL) was added mCPBA (296
mg, 1.2 mmol; 70 wt%) at 0 °C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 30
min at 0 °C, and then for 5 h at rt. The reaction mixture was filtered
through alumina short column (hexane/AcOEt = 5:1) and concentrated. The
residue was purified with a flash chromatography (SiO2; hexane/AcOEt =
100:1-10:1) to give the epoxide 4a in 95% yield (152 mg). Epoxide (4a):
colorless oil, yield (95 %) IR (neat) 2935, 2861, 1338, 1102, 832 cm-1;
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.25-1.46 (20H, m), 1.56-1.74 (6H, m), 2.47
(1H, dd, J = 5.0, 2.8 Hz), 2.74 (1H, dd, J = 5.0, 5.0 Hz), 2.94 (1H, m),
3.38 (1H, tt, J = 7.1, 3.5 Hz), 3.42-3.49 (2H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 20.6, 23.0, 23.1, 24.2, 24.6, 26.6, 28.8, 29.4, 47.1, 52.2,
67.8, 77.0; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C17H32O2Na [M+Na]+ 291.2295, found
291.2291.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM CCl3CN: A crucial promoter of mCPBA-mediated direct ether oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kamijo, Shin; Matsumura, Shoko; Inoue, Masayuki
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(18), 4195-4197

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME219 STEP1
