$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Epoxidation of
Oxazolidines 1 with meta-Chloroperbenzoic Acid (mCPBA). A sample of the
particular olefin 1 was dissolved in CDCl3 and 1.1 equiv. mCPBA was
added. After 2 h (complete conversion of the olefin), the solution was
filtered to remove the precipitated meta-Chlorobenzoic acid, potassium
carbonate (ca. 200 mg) was added, and the mixture -stirred at 20°C for 30
min. The solids were removed by filtration and the product distribution
was determined by 'H-NMR spectroscopy. The quantitative results are
listed in Table S-1. mCPBA Epoxidation of Olefin 1b. According to the
above general procedure, 79.2 mg (216 μmol) of lb was epoxidized by mCPBA
to yield 78.6 mg (95%) of {2S-[2 α (R*),4 α ]}- and {2S-[2 α (S*),4 α
]}-2-(3,3-dimethyloxiranyl)-N-(4-nitrophenyl)-4-phenyl-3-oxazolidine-carboxamide
(lk-4b and ul-4b) as diastereomeric mixture. {2S-[2 α (S*),4 α
]}-Diastereomer (ul-4b, Minor Diastereomer). 1H NMR δ 1.42 (s, 3 H), 1.57
(s, 3H), 3.22 (d, J = 5.0Hz, 1 H), 4.20 (dd, J = 8.8, 7.5Hz, 1H), 4.50
(dd, J = 9.0, 7.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.88 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 5.65 (d, J = 5.0
Hz, 1 H), 6.74 (s, 1 H), 7.3-8.3 (m, overlap with signals of the like
diastereomer); 13C NMR S 18.4, 24.9, 60.2, 60.9, 63.4, 75.0, 87.8, 118.0,
126.5, 128.1, 129.7, 130.0, 137.2, 144.2, 144.5, 152.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Control of the Diastereoselectivity and Regioselectivity in the
Singlet-Oxygen Ene Reaction of Chiral Oxazolidine-Substituted Alkenes by
a Remote Urea NH Functionality: Comparison with Dimethyldioxirane and
m-Chloroperbenzoic Acid Epoxidations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
