$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Epoxidation of
Oxazolidines 1a-f with Dimethyldioxirane. A sample of the particular
olefin 1 was dissolved in acetone and 1.1 equiv. of a 0.05 - 0.08 M
solution of dimethyldioxirane in acetone were added. After stirring at
20°C for 5 h, the solvent was removed (20°C, 30 mbar) and the product
distribution was determined by IH- NMR spectroscopy. The spectral data
for the epoxides 4a-f are given below and the individual results are
listed in Table 2 (see main text). {2S-[2 α (2R*,3R*),4 α
]}-2-(3-Ethyloxiranyl)-4,N-diphenyl-3-oxazolidinecarboxamide (lk-4d) by
DMD Epoxidation. According to the above general procedure, 21.8 mg (67.6
μmol) of olefin 1d was epoxidized by DMD. Chromatography on the
Chromatotron (5:1 petroleum ether/ethyl ether .mixture as eluent) yielded
21.6 mg (94%) of {2S-[2 α (2R*,3R*),4 α
]}-2-(3-Ethyloxiranyl)-4,N-diphenyl-3-oxazolidinecarboxamide(lk-4d) a
colorless needles. mp 158-159°C. [α]D25 = +49.6° (c 0.51, CHCl3); IR
(KBr) 3344, 3036, 2973, 2879, 1682, 1601, 1548, 1499, 1445, 1334, 1252,
1177, 1082, 1030, 989, 956, 918; 1H NMR δ 1.17 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3 H),
1.7-1.9 (m, 2 H), 3.2-3.3 (m, 2 H), 4.23 (dd, J = 8.8, 4.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.32
(dd, J = 8.9, 6.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.03 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1 H), 5.48 (dd, J = 6.2,
4.1 Hz, 1 H), 6.9-7.5 (m, 10 H), 8.00 (s, 1 H); 13C NMR δ 10.4 (q), 21.2
(t), 58.0 (d, C-8 or C-9), 59.6 (d, C-8 or C-9), 60.2 (d), 73.2 (t), 87.8
(d), 119.2 (d), 123.0 (d), 126.4 (d), 127.6 (d), 128,7 (d), 128.8 (d),
139.0 (s), 140.4 (s), 153.7 (s); Anal. Caled. for C20H22N2O3 (338.4): C,
70.99.; H, 6.55; N 8.28. Found: C, 71.02; H, 6.44; N 7.88.
