$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 2 (GP 2): Epoxidation of
Olefins by m-CPBA: The olefin (2.00 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (20
mL). At 0 °C m-CPBA (518 mg, 3.00 mmol) was added. The mixture was
stirred at room temperature for the indicated time. After adding of Et2O
(50 mL) the mixture was washed with 2N NaOH (2x10 mL), the combined
aqueous layers were extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine (5 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvents were
removed under reduced pressure and the crude product purified by SiO2
chromatography. 4-Methyl-4-(2-propyl-oxiranyl)-pent-2-enoic acid
tert-butyl ester (26): According to GP 2 S8 (834 mg, 3.50 mmmol) and
m-CPBA (1.12 g (77 %), 5.00 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (35 mL) for 3 h. SiO2
chromatography (CH:EE 95:5) gave 26 (835 mg, 94 %). Rf=0.4 (CH:EE 95:5).
1H NMR (300 MHz, C6D6): δ= 7.17 (d, 3 J H-H=15.8 Hz, 1H), 5.90 (d, 3 J
H-H=16.0 Hz, 1H), 2.31 (d, 2 J H-H=4.3 Hz, 1H), 2.17 (d, 2 J H-H=4.3 Hz,
1H), 1.35-1.52 (m, 2H), 1.41 (s, 9H), 1.15-1.21 (m, 1H), 0.88-1.01 (m,
1H), 0.86 (s, 3H(, 0.81 (s, 3H), 0.68 (t, 3 J H-H=7.3 Hz, 3H).13C NMR (75
MHz, C6D6): δ= 165.9, 153.8, 121.6, 79.8, 62.0, 47.3, 40.3, 32.4, 28.2,
23.1, 22.5, 17.7, 14.4. IR (neat): ν= 2970, 1715, 1650, 1470, 1365, 1315,
1255, 1160, 970, 945, 895, 855, 830, 800, 770, 725 cm-1. HRMS: (EI, 70
eV): m/z calcd. for C11H18O2 [M-C 4 H 8]+: 198.1256, found 198.1256 [M-C
4 H 8]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
