$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,2-Dimethyl-3-phenyloxirane (7a) To a stirred solution of
(2-methylprop-1-enyl)benzene (6a) (1.50 g, 11.3 mmol, 1.00 eq.) in DCM
(50 mL), MCPBA (3.07 g, 70%, 12.43 mmol, 1.10 eq.) were added slowly at 0
°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 3 d and then diluted with
pentane (50 mL). The organic layer was washed with sat. aq. NaHCO3 (3 ×
50 mL) and sat. aq. NaCl (1 × 50 mL), dried over MgSO4 and the solvent
was removed under reduced pressure. Purification by column chromatography
(SiO2, hexanes/Et2O 5:1) gave the title compound 7a as a yellow liquid
(1.57 g, 94%). C10H12O (148.20 g mol−1) 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.37-7.26 (m, 5H, Ar-CH), 3.87 (s, 1H, (CH3)2CCH), 1.49 (s, 3H, CH3),
1.08 (s, 3H, CH3’) ppm. 13C{1H}-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 136.7 (s,
Ar-C), 128.1 (s, Ar-C), 127.5 (s, Ar-CCHCHCH), 126.5 (s, Ar-CH), 64.7 (s,
(CH3)2CCH), 61.2 (s, C(CH3)2), 24.9 (s, CH3), 18.1 (s, CH3’) ppm. IR
(NaCl): = 3062m, 3032m, 2963s, 2927s, 1956w, 1889w, 1769w, 1604m, 1496m,
1452s, 1381s, 1322m, 1246s, 1117m, 1032m, 910m, 850m, 799m, 743s, 700s,
624m cm−1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 148 (48), 147 (34), 133 (18), 119
(19), 107 (12), 105 (41), 91 (53), 90 (100), 89 (45), 79 (18), 77 (20).
Elemental analysis calc. (%) for C10H12O: C 81.04, H 8.16; found: C
80.82, H 8.32. Rf = 0.53 (SiO2, hexanes/Et2O 5:1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
