$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedures for the Asymmetric Epoxidation of Olefins. A solution of L2
(0.01 M solution in CH3CN, 1 mL, 0.01 mmol) was added to Fe(OTf)2 (0.01
mmol) at room temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 8 h. To the solution of iron complex was directly added
substrate (0.1 mmol) and CH3CN (0.5 mL) and the mixture was cooled to-20
°C. Then 30% CH3CO3H (0.2 mmol, diluted with 0.1 mL CH3CN) or 75% m-CPBA
(0.2 mmol) was rapidly added and the mixture was stirred at-20 °C for 2.0
h. At this point, a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (8 mL) was added
and the resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc (10 mL× 3). The
organic layer was combined and washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated at reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography to afford the corresponding epoxide.
3'-phenyl-3,4-dihydro-1H-spiro[naphthalene-2,2'-oxiran]-1-one (2a). White
solid, purified by column chromatography on silica gel (15% EtOAc in
petroleum ether) (23.3 mg, 93% yield, 85% ee). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.12 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (m, 1H), 7.37 (m, 6H), 7.24 (m, 2H), 4.37
(s, 1H), 2.92-2.72 (m, 2H), 2.54-2.37 (m, 1H), 1.86 (m, 1H); 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.6, 143.4, 134.2, 132.7, 128.7, 128.4, 128.3, 127.7,
127.0, 126.7, 64.3, 64.1, 27.4, 25.4; HRMS (ESI-TOF) m/z calcd for
C17H14O2 [M+H]+ 251.1072, found 251.1057; HPLC (DAICEL AD-H,
hexane/isopropanol 95:5, flow rate: 1.0 mL/min, 254 nm): tr (major) =
16.5 min, tr (minor) =20.6 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ee=85%, in-situ generated catalyst, optimization study
(ligand, oxidant)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Porphyrin-Inspired Iron Catalyst for Asymmetric Epoxidation of
Electron-Deficient Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
