$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedures for the Asymmetric Epoxidation of
Olefins. A solution of L2 (0.01 M solution in CH3CN, 1 mL, 0.01 mmol) was
added to Fe(OTf)2 (0.01 mmol) at room temperature. The reaction mixture
was stirred at room temperature for 8 h. To the solution of iron complex
was directly added substrate (0.1 mmol) and CH3CN (0.5 mL) and the
mixture was cooled to-20 °C. Then 30% CH3CO3H (0.2 mmol, diluted with 0.1
mL CH3CN) or 75% m-CPBA (0.2 mmol) was rapidly added and the mixture was
stirred at-20 °C for 2.0 h. At this point, a saturated aqueous solution
of NaHCO3 (8 mL) was added and the resulting mixture was extracted with
EtOAc (10 mL× 3). The organic layer was combined and washed with brine,
dried over MgSO4 and concentrated at reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to afford the corresponding
epoxide.
3'-(2-fluoro-4-methylphenyl)-3,4-dihydro-1H-spiro[naphthalene-2,2'-oxiran]-1-one
(2u). White solid, purified by column chromatography on silica gel (15%
EtOAc in petroleum ether) (25.9 mg, 92% yield, 92% ee). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 8.12 (dd, J = 7.8, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (m, 1H), 7.37 (m, 1H), 7.25
(m, 2H), 7.00 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (m, 1H), 4.41 (s, 1H), 2.89 (m,
2H), 2.47-2.40 (m, 1H), 2.38 (s, 3H), 1.75 (m, 1H); 13C {1H} NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.2, 162.3, 161.1 (J = 246 Hz), 143.5, 140.7, 134.2,
132.7, 128.7, 128.2, 127.7, 127.0, 124.7, 118.8, 118.7, 115.9, 115.7,
64.0, 59.8, 27.5, 25.8, 21.2; HRMS (ESI-TOF) m/z calcd for C18H15FO2
[M+H]+ 283.1134, found 283.1137; HPLC (DAICEL AD-H, hexane/isopropanol
95:5, flow rate: 1.0 mL/min, 254 nm): tr (major) = 15.7 min, tr (minor) =
23.0 min.
