$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Epoxidation of Oxazolidines 1 with
meta-Chloroperbenzoic Acid (mCPBA). A sample of the particular olefin 1
was dissolved in CDCl3 and 1.1 equiv. mCPBA was added. After 2 h
(complete conversion of the olefin), the solution was filtered to remove
the precipitated meta-Chlorobenzoic acid, potassium carbonate (ca. 200
mg) was added, and the mixture -stirred at 20°C for 30 min. The solids
were removed by filtration and the product distribution was determined by
'H-NMR spectroscopy. The quantitative results are listed in Table S-1.
mCPBA Epoxidation of Olefin 1a. According to the above general procedure,
51.3 mg (159 μmol) of la was epoxidized by mCPBA to afford 49.5 mg (92%)
of {2S-[2 α (R*),4 α ]}- and {2S-[2 α (S*),4 α
]}-2-(3,3-dimethyloxiranyl)-4,N-diphenyl-3-oxazolidinecarboxamide (lk- 4a
and ul-4a) as diastereomeric mixture. {2S-[2 α (S*),4 α ]}-Diastereomer
(ul-4a, Minor Diastereomer). 1H NMR δ 1.42 (s, 3 H), 1.57 (s, 3 H), 3.20
(d, J = 5.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.16 (dd, J = 8.8, 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.48 (dd, J = 8.8,
6.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.85 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.64 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.16
(s, 1 H), 6.9-7.6 (m, overlap with signals of the like diastereomer); 13C
NMR δ 19.1, 25.0, 60.0, 61.1, 63.7, 75.1, 87.9, 119.5, 123.4, 126.9,
128.8, 129.4, 129.8, 137.9, 138.0, 153.7. The spectral data for the like
diastereomer lk-4a are given above under the DMD epoxidation.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Control of the Diastereoselectivity and Regioselectivity in the
Singlet-Oxygen Ene Reaction of Chiral Oxazolidine-Substituted Alkenes by
a Remote Urea NH Functionality: Comparison with Dimethyldioxirane and
m-Chloroperbenzoic Acid Epoxidations
