$DATUM General Procedure for the Epoxidation with meta-Chloroperbenzoic acid
(mCPBA). A sample of the alkene was dissolved in CDCl3 and 1.1 equiv.
mCPBA was added. After 2 h (complete conversion of the olefin), the
solution was filtered, potassium carbonate (ca. 200 mg) was added, and
stirred at 20 °C for 30 min. The solids were removed by filtration and
the product distribution was determined by 1H-NMR spectroscopy. The
individual results are listed in Table 1 (see main text). mCPBA
Epoxidation of Olefin 1a. According to the general procedure, 51.3 mg
(159 μmol) of 1a was epoxidized by mCPBA to afford 495 mg (92%) of
{2S-[2α(R*),4α]}-and
{2S-[2α(S*),4α]}-2-(3,3-dimethyloxiranyl)-4,N-diphenyl-3-oxazolidinecarboxamide
2a as diastereomeric mixture. {2S-[2α(S*),4α]} (unlike) Diastereomer 2a..
1H NMR δ 1.42 (s, 3 H), 1.57 (s, 3 H), 3.20 (d, J = 5.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.16
(dd, J = 8.8, 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.48 (dd, J = 8.8, 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.85 (t, J =
7.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.64 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.16 (s, 1 H), 6.9-7.6 (m,
overlap with signals of the other diastereomer); 13C NMR δ 19.1, 25.0,
60.0, 61.1, 63.7, 75.1, 87.9, 119.5, 123.4, 126.9, 128.8, 129.4, 129.8,
137.9, 138.0, 153.7.
