$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Epoxidation of
Oxazolidines 1a-f with Dimethyldioxirane. A sample of the particular
olefin 1 was dissolved in acetone and 1.1 equiv. of a 0.05 - 0.08 M
solution of dimethyldioxirane in acetone were added. After stirring at
20°C for 5 h, the solvent was removed (20°C, 30 mbar) and the product
distribution was determined by IH- NMR spectroscopy. The spectral data
for the epoxides 4a-f are given below and the individual results are
listed in Table 2 (see main text). {2S-[2 α (2R*,3S*),4 α
]}-2-(3-Ethyl-3-methyloxiranyl)-N,4-diphenyl-3-oxazolidinecarboxamide
(lk-trans-4f) by DMD Epoxidation. A sample of 168 mg (500 μmol) of E-1f
was epoxidized by DMD according to the above general procedure. The crude
product was purified on the Chromatotron (4:1 petroleum ether/ether
mixture as eluent) to yield 160 mg (91%) of {2S-[2 α (2R*,3S*),4 α
]}-2-(3-ethyl-3-methyloxiranyl)-N,4-diphenyl-3-oxazolidine- carboxamide
(lk-trans-4f) as colorless needles. mp 115-117°C. (a = +46.9° (c 0.91,
CHCl3); IR (KBr): 3323, 2977, 2873, 1678, 1601, 1553, 1502, 1466, 1448,
1340, 1321, 1250, 1170, 1117, 1085,. 1032, 992, 960, 916; 1H NMR δ 1.02
(t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3 H) 1.53 (s, 3 H), 1.5-1.9 (m, 2 H), 3.01 (d, J = 8.2
Hz, 1 H), 4:24 (dd, J = 8.8, 4.0Hz, 1H), 4.32 (dd, J = 8.8, 6.6Hz, 1H),
5.03 (d, J = 8.2Hz, 1H), 5.47 (dd, J = 6.2, 4.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.9-7.5 (m, 10
H), 8.05 (s, 1 H); 13C NMR δ 9.0 (q), 16.5 (q), 31.0 (t), 59.7 (d), 63.3
(d), 64.8 (s), 73.3 (t), 88.5 (d), 119.3 (d), 122.9 (d), 126.4 (d), 127.6
(d), 128.7 (d), 128.8 (d), 139.1 (s), 140.5 (s), 153.8 (s); Anal. Caled.
for C21H24N3O5 (352.4): C, 71.57; H, 6.86; N, 7.95. Fouild: C, 71.74; H,
7.06; N, 8.05.
